<!--Post: 7286--><!--Time: 1108363197-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Metalhead<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Metalhead<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 10:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->WHY WOULD BTK WALK TO HIS VICTIMS HOUSES AND THEN SOMETIMES&#40;AT LEAST ONCE&#41; TAKE THEIR CARS?IT WOULD SEEM THAT SOMEBODY AROUND THE NEIGHBORHOODS WOULD SEE A STRANGER PARK THEIR CAR ON THEIR STREET AND START WALKING AWAY AND THEN COME BACK FOR IT.MAYBE HE ALWAYS PARKED IN A STORES LOT BUT IT WOULD SEEM SOMEBODY THERE WOULD SEE HIM WALKING AWAY CARRYING A BAG?GRANTED IT IS NOT SOMETHING YOU PAY ATTENTION TO BUT IF A MURDER TOOK PLACE IN THE VICINITY IT SEEMS LIKE IT WOULD JOG SOMEONES MEMORY.MAYBE HE HAD CAR TROUBLE AFTER ONE OF HIS DEEDS AND SOMEONE HAD TO GIVE HIM A JUMP!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7286-->
<!--Post: 7300--><!--Time: 1108381118-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7300"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Newyorker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Newyorker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:38 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->completley disagree, he did that to taunt police and say, &#34;hey, i&#39;m walking in broad daylight, kill a whole family in broad daylight, i&#39;m on foot and probably passed by hundreds upon hundreds of local citizens ... they&#39;ve all seen me before and yet you still can&#39;t find me ... what now ? &#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7300-->
<!--Post: 7303--><!--Time: 1108386970-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7303"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 5:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He may have parked at a park, got out for a walk, nothing notable in that. <BR> <BR>He may have parked at a store, gone inside, come out 5 minutes later and acted like he walked to store and just left on foot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7303-->
<!--Post: 7356--><!--Time: 1108421487-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7356"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 2:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Or he may have not had a car at all but instead took public transportation. The bus.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7356-->
<!--Post: 7363--><!--Time: 1108424788-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7363"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Elsbarn<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Elsbarn<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 3:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The MO-ID-RUSE puzzle uses the word &#34;cruise&#34; and I believe this suggests that he canvassed the neighborhoods in a vehicle prior to finding his target&#40;s&#41;. I would think he did this so that he could learn more about them, like when the husbands left in the Otero and Wegerle cases. He probably parked his car where he took the victims&#39; cars and made a quick switch over. <BR> <BR>Getting stopped walking to the scene with the murder kit would not have been as threatening as leaving the scene with the murder kit and mementos &#40;he could always abort if he was stopped on the way to the scene but if stopped once leaving, he would like the kid with his hand stuck in the cookie jar&#41;. <BR> <BR>Basically, I think it was just a result of his fear of getting caught that he took the Otero and  Wegerle cars and part of a plan he had worked out well in advance. These are also cases where he had to work out a &#34;ruse&#34; to gain entry. <BR> <BR>In the evening cases, Anna Williams and Nancy Fox, he broke in and he waited for the women to come home. Here the MO changes, and BTK may have felt comfortable in the darkness to walk home without doing the car switch.  <BR> <BR>Vian does appear to be a crime of opportunity and BTK took some major chances here. By following the young boy home, at least to me, it shows some thinking on BTK’s part that a mother would be available. <BR> <BR>As some serial killers have targeted prostitutes as an outlet for their anger against women, BTK chose mothers. Fox and Bright fall outside of this spectrum—and these two appear to me to have a resemblance to each other, both cute young girls with similar blond bob haircuts. <BR> <BR>There may be two distinct victimologies occurring here. It appears to me to go Mother &#40;Otero&#41;, Single Girl &#40;Bright&#41;, Mother &#40;Vian&#41;, Single Girl &#40;Fox&#41;, Mother &#40;Wegerle&#41;. He still needs to bind them &#40;his signature&#41; but I think BTK has some real issues with his mother firstly and women in general. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7363-->
<!--Post: 7522--><!--Time: 1108550679-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7522"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suspiria_2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suspiria_2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 2:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->the area shown on the maps seems so tight, he could have walked entirely! <BR> <BR>although i think that unlikely... <BR> <BR>slightly veering off topic, perhaps his ruse was used multiple times on some of the victims.  perhaps he had gained entry into one or another of their homes using these ruses prior to coming back in his genuine attack as an effort to case the place first.  if one was relying on being able to obtain access to someone else&#39;s home using various disguises or ruses, wouldn&#39;t it make sense to at least test it out first in a less risky way? <BR> <BR>my reference here being the Boston strangler and his Green Man or Measuring Man crimes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7522-->
<!--Post: 8244--><!--Time: 1109012987-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8244"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 21, 2005 - 11:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->It seems clear that BTK drove part-way and walked part-way to Otero and Wegerly, because: <BR> <BR>1.  Park at the victim&#39;s home and someone may recognize the car/tag.  So BTK parks away from the scene and walks in. <BR> <BR>2.  Using their cars to get to his car makes sense if he drove and parked at a distance.  <BR>Otherwise why drive their cars away, if he has to turn around and walk back to his own car? <BR> <BR>3.  So if he doesn&#39;t take their car then: <BR> <BR>      a.  He walked the whole distance, or <BR>      b.  He had a form of transportation that didn&#39;t require parking &#40;bus, cab&#41;, or <BR>      c.  The victim had no car, or <BR>      d.  Something prevented him from taking their car. <BR> <BR>Public transportation means a driver and/or riders who may recognize him.  He is also at the mercy of their timeliness for his getaway. <BR> <BR>In the daytime, cars hide him; at nightdark hides him.  There&#39;s less risk of being recognized. <BR> <BR>At night he might be walking to his car, or he might be walking home. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:Whoisbtk@yahoo.com">Whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a>  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 8244-->
